he's accused of terrible crimes during  kosovo's war for independence from  serbia in the late 1990s but as he  became the first to stand trial in this  special tribunal in the netherlands  saleh mustafa rejected the charges  telling the judge i'm not guilty of the  counts brought here before me by this  gestapo office  in april 1999 mustafa was a commander in  the rebel kosovo liberation army the kla  the prosecution says he was responsible  for the torture of at least six people  and the murder of one person at a  detention compound  it says the victims were accused by  kosovo's ethnic albanian rebels of  collaborating with serbs or not  supporting the kla  these people  they were not enemies of the state of  kosovo  they were not spies  they were fellow community members  innocent  kosovar albanians whose only crime was  to be viewed  for one reason or another as an  impediment to the kla in certain of its  leaders  the kosovo war is believed to have  killed more than 13 000 people it ended  in 1999 after the nato alliance carried  out 11 weeks of airstrikes against  serbian forces  a former deputy prime minister and five  top former serbian military and police  officials were found guilty of war  crimes committed during the conflict  that was at the un tribunal for the  former yugoslavia  but on wednesday the prosecutors said  the saleh mustafa hearing was a  milestone for this court which has taken  six years to bring anyone to trial this  was one of the failings of the  international criminal tribunal  for former yugoslavia not to be able to  really sentence any uh kosovo liberation  army uh soldiers and commanders where it  was clear that some war crimes had been  committed not to the same scale and  intensity as those by the serbian army  that is quite clear but they had also  committed war crimes the new court's  activities are highly sensitive in  kosovo where former rebel commanders  still dominate political life  in june 2020 then president hashim  thatchy was indicted for his alleged  role in nearly a hundred murders while  he led the kla he's currently being held  in the hague awaiting trial nadim baba  al-jazeera
 

